id: SCA-067
title: Environment variable exfiltration pattern
category: supply-chain
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .sh .bash .py .js .ts .rb
  exclude_paths: test/ node_modules/ .git/ vendor/
patterns:
  - regex: (curl|wget)\s+.*(\$ENV|\$\{.*TOKEN|process\.env|os\.environ|ENV\[)
    message: Environment variables (often containing secrets, tokens, CI credentials) being sent to external server via curl/wget — strong indicator of credential theft.
  - regex: (requests|fetch|http)\s*.*(\$ENV|process\.env|os\.environ|ENV\[)
    message: Environment variables being sent via HTTP — possible credential exfiltration.
fix: Environment variables should never be sent to external hosts. This is a strong indicator of credential theft. Investigate immediately.
